@startuml
' =============================================================================
' Multi-account deployment — organization, organizational units, accounts and the pipeline
' UML deployment diagram
'
' Mermaid source set : diagrams/mermaid/25-multi-account-aws.md is planned and not yet
'                      written. This view is built from 03-architecture-patterns/README.md
'                      (the multi-account pattern), ARCHITECTURE-DECISIONS.md ADR-013
'                      (one AWS account per environment), ADR-011 (state per environment),
'                      ADR-014 (OIDC, Actions pinned by commit SHA), and the chapters
'                      00-foundations/aws-fundamentals/05-organizations-control-tower.md and
'                      04-infrastructure-as-code/terraform/04-state-backends-locking.md.
'                      Diagram sets 18 and 21 supply the guardrail-enforcement and SCP facts.
' Verified           : 2026-11-15
' Status             : academy design, not an official AWS reference architecture.
'                      OU names and the placement of the state bucket are academy choices.
'                      No AWS icons; nothing is included from the network.
'
' Official sources this view relies on:
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_getting-started_concepts.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_bedrock.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_integrate_delegated_admin.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/how-control-tower-works.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/account-factory.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/cross-region-inference.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-enforcements.html
'   https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/backend/s3
'   https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials/main/README.md
'
' What UML adds: accounts as execution nodes inside organizational units, and the
' pipeline's role chain as numbered communication paths.
' =============================================================================
!pragma layout smetana
title Multi-account generative AI platform — organization, accounts and deployment pipeline (UML deployment)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam noteBorderColor #888888
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam legendBorderColor #888888
skinparam nodesep 50
skinparam ranksep 60

!$CLIENT   = "#E8F1FB;line:1F6FEB;text:0B1F33"
!$COMPUTE  = "#FDEBD0;line:D97706;text:3B2300"
!$AI       = "#E6F4EA;line:1E8E3E;text:0B2E13"
!$DATA     = "#EDE7F6;line:6A1B9A;text:2A0A3D"
!$SECURITY = "#FDECEA;line:C62828;text:3D0A0A"
!$OBS      = "#FFF8E1;line:B28704;text:3D2E00"
!$EXTERNAL = "#F1F3F4;line:5F6368;line.dashed;text:202124"

actor "Developer" as dev $CLIENT
actor "Platform administrator" as admin $CLIENT

node ci $EXTERNAL [
  <b>CI service, for example GitHub Actions</b>
  ----
  OIDC identity provider · no long-lived AWS keys
  third-party Actions pinned by full commit SHA
]

frame "AWS Organization · all features enabled" as org {

  node mgmt $SECURITY [
    <b>Management account</b>
    ----
    AWS Organizations: root, OUs, SCPs, Amazon Bedrock policies
    AWS Control Tower: landing zone, controls, Account Factory
    AWS IAM Identity Center: single sign-on
    ----
    not restricted by SCPs or RCPs · keep it empty of workloads
  ]

  frame "Security OU" as secOu {
    node logAcct $OBS [
      <b>Log archive account</b>
      ----
      Amazon S3: organization trail log files
    ]
    node auditAcct $SECURITY [
      <b>Audit account</b>
      ----
      AWS Config aggregator
      delegated administrator for security services
    ]
  }

  frame "Shared services OU (academy naming)" as sharedOu {
    node toolAcct $COMPUTE [
      <b>Deployment (tooling) account</b>
      ----
      pipeline role, assumed through OIDC
      ----
      Terraform state bucket: one state object per
      environment and component · use_lockfile ·
      versioning · SSE-KMS
    ]
  }

  frame "Workloads — non-production OU\nSCP: Region deny with an inference-profile exception" as nonProdOu {
    node devAcct $AI [
      <b>Development account</b>
      ----
      deploy role trusts the tooling account
      application · Amazon Bedrock Runtime
    ]
    node testAcct $AI [
      <b>Test account</b>
      ----
      deploy role trusts the tooling account
      application · Amazon Bedrock Runtime
    ]
    node stagingAcct $AI [
      <b>Staging account</b>
      ----
      deploy role trusts the tooling account
      application · Amazon Bedrock Runtime
    ]
  }

  frame "Workloads — production OU\nSCP · Amazon Bedrock policy: enforced guardrail" as prodOu {
    node prodAcct $AI [
      <b>Production account</b>
      ----
      deploy role trusts the tooling account
      application · Amazon Bedrock Runtime
      Bedrock quotas per account and Region:
      test load cannot starve production
    ]
  }
}

dev --> ci : 1. pull request · merge
ci --> toolAcct : 2. assume the pipeline role\nthrough OIDC
toolAcct --> devAcct : 3. assume deploy role\napply · dev
toolAcct --> testAcct : 4. promote · test
toolAcct --> stagingAcct : 5. promote · staging
toolAcct --> prodAcct : 6. promote · production\n(approval gate: academy recommendation)
admin --> mgmt : sign in · enable controls\nrequest accounts
mgmt ..> nonProdOu : SCPs inherited by every account
mgmt ..> prodOu : SCPs and Amazon Bedrock policy inherited
prodAcct ..> logAcct : organization trail · log files
prodAcct ..> auditAcct : AWS Config compliance data

note as nState
  <b>Pipeline run (steps 3 to 6)</b>
  The run reads and writes its environment's
  state object and a .tflock lock object, then
  applies in the target account with that
  account's deploy role. Each environment has its
  own state and its own deploy role (ADR-011, ADR-013)
end note

legend right
  |= Notation |= Meaning |
  | frame | organization or organizational unit (OU) |
  | node | AWS account (execution environment) |
  | solid arrow, numbered | deployment path: role assumption and apply |
  | dashed arrow | policy inheritance or log delivery |
  |<#F1F3F4> grey dashed | outside AWS |
  |<#FDECEA> red | governance and security accounts |
  |<#FDEBD0> orange | deployment tooling |
  |<#E6F4EA> green | workload accounts running Amazon Bedrock |
  |<#FFF8E1> yellow | log archive |
  SCP deny at any level wins for every account below. A Geographic profile needs every
  destination Region allowed; a Global profile needs aws:RequestedRegion "unspecified".
  Every workload account delivers trail logs and Config data; arrows drawn for production only.
  Academy design · not an official AWS diagram · Verified 2026-11-15
endlegend
@enduml
